        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: പത്രപ്രവർത്തകൻ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പത്രപ്രവർത്തകൻ — patrapravarttakan — \"a journalist\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "എന്റെ അമ്മാവൻ ഒരു പത്രപ്രവർത്തകൻ ആണ്. enṟe ammāvan oru patrapravarttakan āṇŭ. My uncle is a journalist."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A woman journalist is പത്രപ്രവർത്തക. പത്രപ്രവർത്തനം, journalism, is the trade."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പത്രപ്രവർത്തകൻ (patrapravarttakan) is built from പത്രം (patraṁ), \"a newspaper\", and പ്രവർത്തകൻ, \"a worker\", from Sanskrit pravartaka, \"setting in motion, promoting\" (Monier-Williams), the same word as in സഹപ്രവർത്തകൻ, \"a colleague\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
